        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-20T01:52:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t understand this calculation, why is TRNG_SAMPLE_BITS multiplied by 32?\n\nWhat is the meaning of TRNG_SAMPLE_BITS - I thought it was the number of bits from a sample to use, where sample size is 32 bits?\n\nMaybe we should chat about this offline, or maybe a better comment would help.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 64,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "47a66cb244c54b5e50728f774b8684e12e0d1069",
